  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enhancing Capacity to Increase Production and Marketing of High Quality Mild Arabica Coffee</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Karansi AMCOS is a smallholder coffee farmers cooperative located in a marginalized community in Kilimanjaro Region at the border with Mt Meru in Arusha Region. The more than 1700 direct beneficiaries of whom more than 800 are women will increase their incomes and livelihoods through improved coffee production occasioned by improvement in agronomic practices, processing cherry coffee at the central pulping station and pursuing the Speciality Coffee market.</narrative>
  </description>
